[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 1. Isolated Tmux Server Architecture\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H\u001b[K\n The most distinctive technical feature is the use of a \u001b[1mseparate tmux server\u001b(B\u001b[m. Instead of creating a    \u001b[4;37H session on the default tmux server, \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot\u001b[39m uses the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m-L\u001b[39m socket option to start a completely isolated tmux \u001b[5;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[6;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[7;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[8;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[9;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[10;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[13;37H\u001b[K\n The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[16;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[17;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[18;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[19;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[20;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[21;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[23;37H\u001b[K\n The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[25;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[26;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[27;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[28;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[29;37H   changes\u001b[K\u001b[31;37H \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠙\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[34;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[36;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[37;37H\u001b[38;2;142;131;123mLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[34;39H"]
[0.036, "o", "\u001b[1;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 1. Isolated Tmux Server Architecture\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[3;37H The most distinctive technical feature is the use of a \u001b[1mseparate tmux server\u001b(B\u001b[m. Instead of creating a    \u001b[4;37H session on the default tmux server, \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot\u001b[39m uses the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m-L\u001b[39m socket option to start a completely isolated tmux \u001b[5;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[6;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[7;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[8;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[9;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[10;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[12;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[14;37H The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[16;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[17;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[18;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[19;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[20;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[22;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[24;37H The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[25;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[26;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[27;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[28;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[29;37H   changes\u001b[K\u001b[31;37H \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠹\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[34;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[36;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[37;37H\u001b[38;2;142;131;123mLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[34;39H"]
[0.011, "o", "\u001b[1;36H\u001b[38;2;146;131;116m│\u001b[2;36H│\u001b[3;36H│\u001b[4;36H│\u001b[5;36H│\u001b[6;36H│\u001b[7;36H│\u001b[8;36H│\u001b[9;36H│\u001b[10;36H│\u001b[11;36H│\u001b[12;36H│\u001b[13;36H│\u001b[14;36H│\u001b[15;36H│\u001b[16;36H│\u001b[17;36H│\u001b[18;36H│\u001b[19;36H│\u001b[20;36H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;60;56;54m│\u001b[21;36H│\u001b[22;36H│\u001b[23;36H│\u001b[24;36H│\u001b[25;36H│\u001b[26;36H│\u001b[27;36H│\u001b[28;36H│\u001b[29;36H│\u001b[30;36H│\u001b[31;36H│\u001b[32;36H│\u001b[33;36H│\u001b[34;36H│\u001b[35;36H│\u001b[36;36H│\u001b[37;36H│\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[H \u001b[1magents-on-tmux\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[20X\r\n \u001b[1mAgents\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1m(1)\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[2mWindows\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m(1)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[10X\u001b[100m\u001b[2m\r\n▔\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34m\u001b[100m▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔\u001b[39m\u001b[2m▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100m\r\n \u001b[34m* \u001b[39m\u001b[1mpi\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100m\u001b[24X\u001b[24C11s   \u001b[49m\u001b[100m\r\n  Pi       ~/D/R/agents-on-tmux   \u001b[49m\u001b[90m\r\n▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀\u001b[39m\u001b[7;35H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[1mC-a C-a\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m prefix\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1mc\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m new\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1mn\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m next\u001b(B\u001b[m     \r\n \u001b[1mp\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m prev\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1ml\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m last\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1m,\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m rename\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[10X\u001b[1;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 1. Isolated Tmux Server Architecture\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H\u001b[K\n The most distinctive technical feature is the use of a \u001b[1mseparate tmux server\u001b(B\u001b[m. Instead of creating a    \u001b[4;37H session on the default tmux server, \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot\u001b[39m uses the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m-L\u001b[39m socket option to start a completely isolated tmux \u001b[5;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[6;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[7;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[8;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[9;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[10;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[13;37H\u001b[K\n The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[16;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[17;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[18;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[19;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[20;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[21;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[23;37H\u001b[K\n The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[25;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[26;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[27;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[28;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[29;37H   changes\u001b[K\u001b[30;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠹\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[32;37H\u001b[K\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m\n─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m\u001b[34;37H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m\u001b[35;37H───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m\u001b[36;37H⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m\u001b[37;37HLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;2;146;131;116m\u001b[48;2;60;56;54m\u001b[7m\r\n 10 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;146;131;116m\u001b[48;2;60;56;54m\u001b[38;2;250;189;47m\u001b[7m *  aot \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;250;189;47m\u001b[48;2;60;56;54m\u001b[38;2;146;131;116m\u001b[71X\u001b[71C diovani@paulodiovani-thinkpad  Sat 17:28 \u001b[7m ♥♥♥♥♥ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4;32H\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1003l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[1;37H The most distinctive technical feature is the use of a \u001b[1mseparate tmux server\u001b(B\u001b[m. Instead of creating a    \u001b[2;37H session on the default tmux server, \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot\u001b[39m uses the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m-L\u001b[39m socket option to start a completely isolated tmux \u001b[3;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[4;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[5;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[6;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[7;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[8;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[9;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[12;37H The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[13;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[14;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[15;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[16;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[17;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[18;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[19;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[22;37H The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[23;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[24;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[25;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[26;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[27;37H   changes (like restarting an agent or switching windows).\u001b[K\u001b[28;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m### How it Works (Execution\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[31;37H \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠹\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[34;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[36;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[37;37H\u001b[38;2;142;131;123mLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[4;32H"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[1;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[3;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[4;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[5;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[6;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[7;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[10;37H The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[12;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[13;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[14;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[16;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[17;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[20;37H The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[21;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[22;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[23;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[24;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[25;37H   changes (like restarting an agent or switching windows).\u001b[K\u001b[26;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m### How it Works (Execution Flow)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[29;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m1.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[31;37H \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠹\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[34;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[36;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[37;37H\u001b[38;2;142;131;123mLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[4;32H"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[36;2H\u001b[1m↑↓\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m navigat\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1m→\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m windo\u001b[Cs\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1m⏎\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m focus\u001b[37;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1mc\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2mnew\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C\u001b[1m,\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m rename\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1md\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m kill\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C\u001b[1mq\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m quit\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.012, "o", "\u001b[1;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[3;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[4;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[5;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[6;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[8;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[10;37H The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[12;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[13;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[14;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[16;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[18;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[20;37H The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[21;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[22;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[23;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[24;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[25;37H   changes (like restarting an agent or switching windows).\u001b[K\u001b[27;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m### How it Works (Execution Flow)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[29;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mStart:\u001b(B\u001b[m The user\u001b[K\u001b[31;37H \u001b[38;2;203;141;168m⠹\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;170;160;153mWorking\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m─\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;135;175mgemma4:31b-cloud\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m / \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;0;175;175magents-on-tmux \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[34;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[7m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;37H\u001b[38;2;200;132;161m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[36;37H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;95;175;95m⎇ feature/gh-pages \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;142;131;123m5.3%/128k (auto)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[37;37H\u001b[38;2;142;131;123mLSP Inactive\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[16D"]
[0.019, "o", "\u001b[1;37H server instance.\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mPrevention of Freezes:\u001b(B\u001b[m Nested tmux sessions on the same server often conflict or freeze. By using a \u001b[3;37H   separate socket (\u001b[38;2;203;142;168mSOCKET_NAME = \"agents-on-tmux\"\u001b[39m), the \"inner\" session is logically and physically   \u001b[4;37H   separated from the \"outer\" (parent) session.\u001b[K\u001b[5;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSocket Detection:\u001b(B\u001b[m The tool can detect the parent tmux socket via the \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mTMUX\u001b[39m environment variable to   \u001b[6;37H   ensure it interacts correctly with the surrounding environment.\u001b[K\u001b[8;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 2. The Backend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/backends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[10;37H The backend handles the low-level communication with tmux.\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmux\u001b[39m Trait:\u001b(B\u001b[m Defines a clean contract for managing sessions, windows, panes, and key bindings.       \u001b[12;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[1mTmuxDriver\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u001b[m The implementation that executes shell commands. It uses a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mCommandExecutor\u001b[39m trait, which \u001b[13;37H   allows the project to use a \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mShellCommandExecutor\u001b[39m for production and a mock executor for unit        \u001b[14;37H   testing (essential for testing tmux logic without actually needing a tmux server running).\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mAgent Management:\u001b(B\u001b[m It tracks \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mWindow\u001b[39m states, including which command is running, when it started, and \u001b[16;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[18;37H \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\