[m\u001b[2m rename\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[10X\u001b[1;37H   whether it has pending notifications.\u001b[K\u001b[2;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m#### 3. The Frontend (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;203;142;168msrc/frontends/\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[4;37H\u001b[K\n The project provides a TUI for interacting with the agents.\u001b[K\u001b[6;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTUI Interface:\u001b(B\u001b[m Built to be lightweight and theme-aware.\u001b[K\u001b[7;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mTheme Support:\u001b(B\u001b[m It uses ANSI color slots (0-15), ensuring the UI inherits the user's terminal colors \u001b[8;37H   rather than forcing a specific RGB palette.\u001b[K\u001b[9;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mControl Loop:\u001b(B\u001b[m The \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mApp\u001b[39m state manages user actions (mapped via \u001b[38;2;203;142;168mkey_to_action\u001b[39m) to trigger backend      \u001b[10;37H   changes (like restarting an agent or switching windows).\u001b[K\u001b[11;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;210;150;31m\u001b[1m### How it Works (Execution Flow)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[13;37H\u001b[K\n \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mStart:\u001b(B\u001b[m The user runs \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot\u001b[39m (or \u001b[38;2;203;142;168maot --tui\u001b[39m).\u001b[K\u001b[15;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m2. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mEnvironment Setup:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[16;37H     \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39mIt detects if it's already inside its own isolated server to prevent infinite nesting.\u001b[K\u001b[17;37H     \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39mIt creates the isolated tmux server/session if it doesn't exist.\u001b[K\u001b[18;37H \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m3. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mLaunch:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[19;37H     \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mWithout \u001b[38;2;203;142;168m--tui\u001b[39m:\u001b(B\u